<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anantavarman Chodaganga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1078–<a href="/years/1147">1147</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anantavarman Chodaganga was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-ganga-dynasty">Eastern Ganga dynasty</a>, related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> through his mother. In a reign of about seventy years he conquered the Somavamshi kingdom and united the lands from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> to the Godavari, moving his capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a>. He began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a> Temple at Puri, which became the religious centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anantavarman-chodaganga.jpg" alt="Anantavarman Chodaganga" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Deepak Kumar Nayak (Cuttack) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chodaganga_Deva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
